WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.069
-The President is still
holding the government hostage

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.904
over its demands
for a border wall

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.406
as federal employees prepare to
go another week without pay.

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.675
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.279
♪♪

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.248
We are now in day 34
of the government shutdown,

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.217
and the consequences
are very real.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:21.254
More than 800,000 federal
workers are missing paychecks.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.989
The basic everyday functions
of the government

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.390
are grinding to a halt.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.158
Even the eagle
in the presidential seal

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.826
is currently unemployed.

00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:29.829
There are also the crucial
day-to-day functions

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.165
that no one thinks of, the
things we all take for granted

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.733
that are essentially
at a standstill

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.334
thanks to Trump's shutdown.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.969
-800,000 federal workers

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:40.039
on the verge of missing
another paycheck,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.475
workers who,
just like the rest of us,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.010
they have to
feed their families,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.244
they have to pay their rent.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.346
Airports especially hard-hit
right now

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.884
with 10% of TSA screeners
calling in sick

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.485
and air-traffic controllers

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.488
warning planes will just
sit on the ground.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.757
-Critical government services
are also deteriorating.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.026
Food safety inspections
have been curtailed.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.528
The FBI and federal agents
are seeing their cases hampered,

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.497
according to an article
in "The Washington Post."

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.198
There's been a slowdown
in planning

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.468
for hurricanes
and other disasters.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.970
-Think about that.
The Trump administration

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.539
will now be even less prepared
for hurricanes

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:16.809
than they were during this
briefing in the Oval Office.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:20.446
-I've received a briefing
from Secretary Nielsen,

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:23.216
Administrator Long,
and my senior staff

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.784
regarding Hurricane Florence.

00:01:25.784 --> 00:01:28.021
They haven't seen anything
like what's coming at us

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:33.459
in 25, 30 years, maybe ever.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.462
It's tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.998
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.234
-Well, I mean, at least...

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.369
at least he had two charts
next to him.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.072
I mean, could you imagine
what those charts will say

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:50.943
if there's a hurricane
during the shutdown?

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:55.815
"If I can direct
your attention to 'big.'"

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.785
All of this is happening for one
reason and only one reason --

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.520
Trump's demands that we pay
billions for a border wall

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.856
that he repeatedly said
Mexico would pay for.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:06.359
And Trump's argument
is simple -- walls work.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.761
For example, in the places
where they already exist,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.363
Trump claims walls have had
an immediate impact.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.332
In talking to reporters
this week,

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.968
he named one city in particular

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.536
where a border wall
is making everyone safer.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:20.172
-Everybody knows
that walls work.

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:24.043
You look at different places,
they put up a wall, no problem.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.744
You look at San Antonio.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.481
You look at so many
different places.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:33.819
They go from one of the most
unsafe cities in the country

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.489
to one of the safest cities
immediately.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.125
-There you go.
The proof is in San Antonio.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.859
They have a border wall,
and it works.

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:42.161
There's just one problem.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:46.366
San Antonio is 150 miles
away from the border.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.401
Either...

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:53.573
Either he is confusing it
with San Diego

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:56.809
or he's just putting walls
in random cities now.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.712
"Walls work, folks.
Just take New York City.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.514
We put one
around the M&amp;M's store,

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:05.884
and it's keeping out
the Times Square Spider-Man."

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:07.553
Trump is the one who said

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.288
he'd be proud
to shut down the government,

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:11.323
and yet after House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi told Trump

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.726
yesterday that she would
postpone the State of the Union

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.796
until the shutdown is over,
Trump blamed her.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:20.066
-We were planning on doing
a really, very important speech

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.635
in front of the House
and the Senate,

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:25.705
the Supreme Court,
and everybody else that's there.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.172
It's called
the State of the Union.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.008
It's in the Constitution.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.409
We're supposed to be doing it,

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:36.015
and now Nancy Pelosi --
or Nancy, as I call her...

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.018
-Oh.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.253
You call her Nancy.

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:43.789
Good burn.

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.991
You're so good with nicknames.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.728
I guess that's why
they call you...

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.730
Donald.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.732
If Trump was your roommate,

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:57.537
he'd label his milk
by writing "milk" on it.

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.238
If he was any less creative,

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.008
this would be the name
of his building.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.642
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.678
Trump then went on to explain

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.514
that he thinks he knows why
Pelosi canceled the speech.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.749
-The State of the Union speech

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:13.452
has been canceled
by Nancy Pelosi

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:15.321
because she doesn't want
to hear the truth.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.555
-Dude, you don't even know

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.492
the truth about
where San Antonio is.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.661
You're afraid of the truth
and maps.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.464
"We built the wall in San
Antonio, folks. It's beautiful.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:27.900
Unfortunately, we did have to
build it on top of San Antonio's

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.703
most famous landmark,
the Golden Gate Bridge."

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.572
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.006
And not only is the shutdown

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.275
paralyzing basic services
people depend on

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.978
and subjecting federal workers
to needless suffering,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.013
it's undercutting
Trump's stated goal

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.015
of securing the border.

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.950
For example,
the FBI says the shutdown

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.885
is hurting its ability
to fight MS-13,

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:49.788
which is crazy because Trump is
obsessed with gangs like MS-13

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:52.024
which he falsely claims
are pouring into the country

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.359
over the Southern border.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.428
Sometimes he even spins
elaborate fantasies

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.830
about towns
that are occupied by MS-13

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.099
and liberated
by law enforcement.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.201
-You know, it's like liberating.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:06.672
Like, a war.
Like there's a foreign invasion.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:09.042
And they occupy your country,

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.611
and then you get them out
through whatever.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:14.047
And they call it liberation.
You're liberated.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.182
And these towns
are being liberated,

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.117
and the people are clapping.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.353
They get them,
they take them out,

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.054
and the people
are in their windows.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.656
They're clapping and screaming,
and they're happy.

00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:26.959
-They're clapping and screaming,
and they're happy?

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.429
Did he accidentally watch
the end of "Return of the Jedi"

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:32.464
and think it was the news?

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:33.633
"And let me tell you.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.235
The little bears,
they're the happiest of all.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.037
They're screaming and clapping
and doing their little dance.

00:05:39.037 --> 00:05:41.808
And one of them said something.
It made a lot of sense to me.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.643
'Yub nub.'"

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.545
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:49.682
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.184
Now, it's not surprising
that Trump lied about the wall

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:53.986
or that he's detached
from the reality

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.854
of what's actually happening
on the border.

00:05:55.854 --> 00:05:58.157
It seems like every week,
we get a new insider account

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.859
about just how unfit he is
for the job

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.428
and how chaotic the
White House is as a result.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.897
The latest account is a tell-all
book called "Team of Vipers"

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.700
by former White House director
of message strategy Cliff Sims.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.969
Sims describes a president

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.071
who's uninterested
in the basic duties of his job

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.139
like a meeting with former
House Speaker Paul Ryan

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:16.542
about the GOP
legislative agenda.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:19.545
-In early 2017, the Speaker
comes up to the White House

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.513
with Mike Pence,
the vice president,

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:24.149
to explain how tax reform
is going to work

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:27.119
in all of its wonderful,
mechanistic detail.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:29.255
This does not interest
the President very much.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.523
And after the conversation's
gone on for a while,

00:06:31.523 --> 00:06:32.625
he literally gets up

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.326
while Paul Ryan
is in mid-description

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:36.862
and wanders
out of the Oval Office

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:39.398
and down the hallway
into a side room

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.435
where one can hear the
television being switched on.

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:45.203
And eventually,
Mike Pence gets up,

00:06:45.203 --> 00:06:48.140
goes down the hall,
brings the President back,

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.176
and they finish
the conversation.

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.544
-Oh, my God.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.146
We have a president who
just wanders around the house

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:57.416
in slow motion no matter
what's going on around him.

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:59.986
It's like we elected a Roomba.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.054
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.023
"Yeah, that's very interesting.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:07.559
Yeah. No. That's really cool.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:09.295
That's really cool."

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.731
[ Applause ]

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.900
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:22.074
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:25.444
Trump was also easily distracted
by random obsessions.

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:27.813
For example, he was preparing
for a televised call

00:07:27.813 --> 00:07:29.882
to the International
Space Station.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.917
He was getting ready
for the call.

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:35.020
Trump suddenly appeared
distracted, distant.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.388
As the clock ticked down,

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.357
Trump suddenly turned toward
the NASA administrator.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.125
He asked,
"What's our plan for Mars?"

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.128
The administrator
explained to the President

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.262
that NASA plans to send a rover
to Mars in 2020

00:07:44.262 --> 00:07:46.565
and by the 2030s would attempt
a manned space flight.

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:48.901
Trump bristled. He asked,
"But is there any way

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.103
we could do it by the end
of my first term?"

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:53.505
Why? Are you trying
to escape somewhere

00:07:53.505 --> 00:07:56.775
that's out of Robert Mueller's
jurisdiction?

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.477
"Mr. President...

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:02.881
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:02.881 --> 00:08:05.751
Mr. President, we have
a warrant for your arrest."

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:10.556
"Oh, yeah? Well, you'll
have to catch me first."

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.025
The story actually
gets weirder, though.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.494
Trump was still distracted
with just minutes to go

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.830
before the live televised call
with the space station.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.399
As he walked with Sims from the
dining room to the Oval Office,

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.401
he decided to stop
in his white-marble bathroom

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.637
for one final check
in the mirror.

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:27.874
He had 30 seconds before
he was supposed to be on camera.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.376
In the bathroom mirror, Trump
smirked and said to himself,

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:33.913
"Space station,
this is your president."

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:35.915
"Space station,
this is your president."

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:39.952
Is he turning into a terrible
David Bowie cover band?

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.921
Of course,
none of this is surprising.

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.889
We could only guess what kind
of politician Trump would be,

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:46.258
but we knew what kind of
employer he would be --
a [bleep] one.

00:08:46.258 --> 00:08:48.527
And he's not even the only
[bleep] boss in the White House.

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:50.762
For example, today one of the
billionaires in Trump's cabinet,

00:08:50.762 --> 00:08:52.064
Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross,

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:53.932
was asked about
the 800,000 federal workers

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:55.800
going without pay
during the shutdown

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.437
and said he couldn't
understand why they
don't just take out loans.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:01.507
And, again, remember,
this man is a billionaire.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:03.743
-There are reports
there are some federal workers

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:07.280
who are going to
homeless shelters to get food.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.583
-I know they are, and I don't
really quite understand why

00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:14.687
because, as I mentioned before,
they --

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:18.190
the obligations
that they would undertake,

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.460
say borrowing from a bank
or a credit union,

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.663
are, in effect,
federally guaranteed.

00:09:24.663 --> 00:09:28.867
So the 30 days of pay
that some people will be out,

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:30.770
there's no real reason

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:34.674
why they shouldn't be able
to get a loan against it.

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:36.442
-Never take financial advice

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:39.412
from someone who appears
next to a stock ticker.

00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:42.314
He does not have
your best interests at heart.

00:09:42.314 --> 00:09:46.085
"Now if you'll excuse me,
my riches!"

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:48.453
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:50.755
The government is paralyzed
by a petulant president

00:09:50.755 --> 00:09:53.059
subjecting millions of people
to needless suffering

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.493
for a wall that won't even work.

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:57.563
Polls have shown that public
opinion is firmly against him

00:09:57.563 --> 00:10:00.332
and firmly on the side
of Nancy Pelosi, or...

00:10:00.332 --> 00:10:03.569
-Nancy, as I call her.
-This has been "A Closer Look."

